sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as Platform Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Dashboard as Ray Dashboard<br/>8265/TCP HTTP
    participant Operator as KubeRay Operator
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant CertMgr as cert-manager<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Head as Ray Head Pod
    participant Workers as Ray Worker Pods
    participant Redis as Redis (GCS FT)<br/>6379/TCP

    Note over Client,Redis: Flow 1: RayCluster Authentication (OIDC via Gateway API)
    Client->>GW: HTTPS/443 — GET /ray/{ns}/{cluster}/<br/>TLS 1.2+ (Gateway-terminated)
    GW->>KRBP: HTTPS/8443<br/>TLS, OIDC token
    KRBP->>KRBP: SubjectAccessReview<br/>(check GET on head-svc)
    KRBP->>Dashboard: HTTP/8265<br/>Loopback (no auth)
    Dashboard-->>KRBP: Dashboard response
    KRBP-->>GW: HTTPS response
    GW-->>Client: HTTPS response

    Note over Client,Redis: Flow 2: RayJob Submission (K8sJobMode)
    Operator->>K8sAPI: HTTPS/443 — Create RayCluster<br/>ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: RayCluster created
    Operator->>K8sAPI: HTTPS/443 — Create Submitter Job<br/>ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Job created
    Note over Operator: Submitter Job Pod starts
    Operator->>Dashboard: HTTP/8265 — POST /api/jobs/<br/>Job submission
    Dashboard-->>Operator: Job ID returned
    Operator->>Dashboard: HTTP/8265 — GET /api/jobs/{id}<br/>Status polling
    Dashboard-->>Operator: Job status

    Note over Client,Redis: Flow 3: RayService Incremental Upgrade (Gateway API Traffic Splitting)
    Client->>GW: HTTPS/443 — Inference request<br/>TLS
    GW->>Head: HTTP/8000 — Active cluster serve-svc<br/>Weight: 90%
    GW->>Workers: HTTP/8000 — Pending cluster serve-svc<br/>Weight: 10%
    Operator->>K8sAPI: HTTPS/443 — Update HTTPRoute weights<br/>ServiceAccount token
    Note over Operator: Gradually shift traffic<br/>active→pending

    Note over Client,Redis: Flow 4: mTLS Certificate Lifecycle
    Operator->>CertMgr: HTTPS/443 — Create SelfSigned Issuer<br/>ServiceAccount token
    CertMgr-->>Operator: Issuer ready
    Operator->>CertMgr: HTTPS/443 — Create CA Certificate<br/>ServiceAccount token
    CertMgr->>K8sAPI: Create CA Secret<br/>{cluster}-ca-secret-{uid}
    Operator->>CertMgr: HTTPS/443 — Create leaf Certificates<br/>(head + worker, 90-day expiry)
    CertMgr->>K8sAPI: Create TLS Secrets<br/>{cluster}-head-cert, {cluster}-worker-cert
    Head->>Workers: gRPC (Ray RPC)<br/>mTLS (cert-manager issued)
    Note over CertMgr: Auto-renewal at<br/>15 days before expiry
